  "context": [
    "The Exter launched in July 2023 on Hyundai's K1 platform, the same architecture shared with the Grand i10 Nios and Aura, positioning it as a micro-SUV between the Grand i10 Nios hatchback and the Venue compact SUV. It is powered by Hyundai's 1.2-litre Kappa petrol engine with a 5-speed manual or AMT, and factory-fitted CNG has been offered on the S and SX trims since launch.",
    "Hyundai made 6 airbags standard across every Exter variant from launch, a notable move in a segment where safety equipment is usually reserved for top trims, and that decision has resonated with safety-conscious resale buyers who increasingly ask about airbag count before purchase.",
    "As one of the newest nameplates in its class, the Exter has limited used-market history beyond its first two to three model years, so resale data is still being established relative to the longer-tenured Venue and Brezza. Early transactions suggest the Exter tracks closely with Hyundai's broader compact-SUV resale pattern, benefiting from the brand's extensive service network and strong buyer trust.",
    "Factory CNG variants hold a firmer resale floor in Delhi NCR, Ahmedabad, and other high gas-penetration markets, consistent with the pattern seen across Hyundai's CNG-equipped lineup, while AMT variants have gained ground steadily against manuals as automatic preference grows among first-time SUV buyers."
  ],
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "What is the resale value of a Hyundai Exter in India?",
      "a": "A well-maintained Exter retains roughly 73% of its ex-showroom price after two years, 65% after three years, and 52% after five years, as of September 2026. For a 2023 petrol SX with 10,000-25,000 km, the current fair-market band is approximately ₹5.97–6.87 lakh."
    },
    {
      "q": "Does Exter CNG hold value better than the petrol version?",
      "a": "Yes, factory CNG Exter units trade at a small but consistent premium over equivalent petrol across the current data, strongest in Delhi NCR and Ahmedabad, reflecting the running-cost advantage that CNG offers in those high-penetration markets."
    },
    {
      "q": "Does the Exter's standard 6-airbag safety package help resale value?",
      "a": "It is a meaningful factor for safety-conscious buyers, and likely contributes to the Exter's five-year retention of about 52%, roughly 4 points above the compact-SUV segment average of 48%."
    },
    {
      "q": "How much does an Exter depreciate per year?",
      "a": "The Exter depreciates roughly 17% in year one and another 10% in year two, before settling into a steadier 6-7% annual decline from year three onward. Ten-year retention sits at around 29%."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which city gives the best resale price for an Exter?",
      "a": "Delhi NCR and Ahmedabad currently trade at +3% above the national mid, driven by strong CNG-variant demand. Kolkata trades at around -2%, where compact-SUV resale cycles run slightly longer."
    }
  ],
